    <name>Amarillo</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[St. Francis and Echo St.<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> Amarillo<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Potter<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> County Seat, Potter County; founded in 1887. Incorporated 1892. Named for Arroyo Amarillo, Spanish name of nearby creek. Transportation, financial, cultural and medical center. Gateway to: Alibates Flint Quarry National Monument, Lake Meredith, Palo Duro State Park, Panhandle-Plains Historic Museum, Boys Ranch. (1965)]]></description>
