  <Placemark>
    <name>Robert E. Lee House</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[Rio Grande City C.I.S.D. campus off US 83. Also known as Commandant's House.<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> Lee Circle, Rio Grande City<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Starr<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> Overlooked steamboat dock on Rio Grande, landscape of northern Mexico. Main rooms were walled with military maps of this locality. Used as field quarters by Col. Robert E. Lee, U.S. Army Commandant in Texas, 1860. Recorded Texas Historic Landmark - 1965]]></description>
